From 20c76ca81a42f8e983d0eb7acaa4e3136190e86b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:04:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): defer temporarily walled independent reviews
 before claim [daveey]

Review dispatch was claiming cards with no independent reviewer available on
this host, then escalating three identical resolution failures into gave_up.

Why 1: route resolution rejected temporary provider walls only after claim.
Why 2: temporary walls/holds and permanent provenance/policy failures shared
ReviewModelUnavailable without a deadline-bearing admission result.
Why 3: preclaim admission checked fresh implementation pins, not independent
review routes; repeated unavailable reviews deliberately exhausted deferrals.
Root (happened): temporary review availability lacked a typed preclaim wait.
Root (not caught): skip tests excluded the review lane without exercising a
complete implementer set whose remaining independent routes were all walled.
Recurrence: Build A and Build B both hit the same three-deferral escalation.

Resolve the same independent routes before claim and record host-local wait
telemetry without creating runs or changing card status/failure budgets.
Track earliest route availability, with max overlapping wall/hold deadlines
per route. Keep structural errors on their existing path. Preserve the typed
temporary refusal through the tier wrapper so a wall racing preflight cannot
exhaust permanent admission deferrals.

Proof:
- Original core source: 8 new dispatch regression cases FAILED.
- Fixed source: 72 files, 1602 tests passed, 0 failed, including 15 new cases.
- scripts/check --base origin/main: all 21 checks passed.
- Cases cover review and downstream ready lanes, provider/pacing/live walls,
  overlap deadlines, unwalled pickup, dry runs, expiry, alternate reviewers,
  registry refusal, structural absence, earliest release and postcheck race.
